Scenario: Sort Changelog Multiple Page Search Results
	Changelog search sorting on multiple pages should work properly

	Given I set the search filters to the "DXP 7.0" product from "Fix Pack 71" to "Fix Pack 76"
	And I go to the Changelog tab
	Then the changelog entry with the content "Error Message after the session expires is not translated" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the content "Reflected XSS in WAIPortlet" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the content "Merge Public Pages results in wrong Navigation Menu" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the content "Security vulnerabilities in Spring core" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the content "AlloyEditor source button fails on Firefox and safari for Mac OS" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the content "Can not create a Data Provider if the default language is set to Spanish" should be visible
	When I go to the next page of the search results
	Then the changelog entry with the content "Publication fails when a Web Content with a Document is displayed in a Web Content Display and an Asset Publisher as well" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the content "JS error when selecting pagination limit" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the content "Same scheduler job may be executed in two threads at the same time" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the content "Unable to acquire state change lock for the module when starting a bundle" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the content "Anchor in portlet url does not work correctly" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the content "Moving a folder with a number of documents takes a long time" should be visible
	When I go to the next page of the search results
	Then the changelog entry with the content "Liferay 7 service-ext.properties not considered" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the content "StagedAuditedModel is not found when using service builder" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the content "Configuration leaking when undeploying bundle" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the content "Update keys and translations made in LPS-85971" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the content "FriendlyURLs are always resolving with the default-language, ignoring the selected language" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the content "Anonymous message boards post can be associated with a user" should be visible
	When I sort the changelog results in ascending order
	Then the current page number of the results page should be page "1"
	And the changelog entry with the content "StagedAuditedModel is not found when using service builder" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the content "Configuration leaking when undeploying bundle" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the content "Update keys and translations made in LPS-85971" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the content "FriendlyURLs are always resolving with the default-language, ignoring the selected language" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the content "Anonymous message boards post can be associated with a user" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the content "Unable to acquire state change lock for the module when starting a bundle" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the content "Anchor in portlet url does not work correctly" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the content "Moving a folder with a number of documents takes a long time" should be visible
	When I go to the next page of the search results
	Then the changelog entry with the content "Liferay 7 service-ext.properties not considered" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the content "JS error when selecting pagination limit" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the content "Same scheduler job may be executed in two threads at the same time" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the content "Publication fails when a Web Content with a Document is displayed in a Web Content Display and an Asset Publisher as well" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the content "AlloyEditor source button fails on Firefox and safari for Mac OS" should be visible
	When I go to the next page of the search results
	Then the changelog entry with the content "Security vulnerabilities in Spring core" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the content "Can not create a Data Provider if the default language is set to Spanish" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the content "Error Message after the session expires is not translated" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the content "Reflected XSS in WAIPortlet" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the content "Merge Public Pages results in wrong Navigation Menu" should be visible
	When I go to the previous page of the search results
	And I sort the changelog results in descending order
	Then the current page number of the results page should be page "1"
	And the changelog entry with the content "Error Message after the session expires is not translated" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the content "Reflected XSS in WAIPortlet" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the content "Merge Public Pages results in wrong Navigation Menu" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the content "Security vulnerabilities in Spring core" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the content "AlloyEditor source button fails on Firefox and safari for Mac OS" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the content "Can not create a Data Provider if the default language is set to Spanish" should be visible
	When I go to the next page of the search results
	Then the changelog entry with the content "Publication fails when a Web Content with a Document is displayed in a Web Content Display and an Asset Publisher as well" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the content "JS error when selecting pagination limit" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the content "Same scheduler job may be executed in two threads at the same time" should be visible
