Scenario: Sort Changelog Refined Search Results
	Changelog search sorting on refined results should work properly

	Given I set the search filters to the "DXP 7.0" product from "Fix Pack 71" to "Fix Pack 76"
	And I go to the Changelog tab
	And I refine the current search using the following refinement criteria
	| Frontend Infrastructure | true |
	Then the changelog entry with the content "AlloyEditor toolbar for table editing is misplaced when content field was half visible" should be in position number "1"
	And the changelog entry with the content "Control Panel Instance Settings fields grayed out after clicking from Account Created Notification" should be in position number "6"
	And the changelog entry with the content "JS error when selecting pagination limit" should be in position number "7"
	And the changelog entry with the content "Anchor in portlet url does not work correctly" should be in position number "9"
	And the changelog entry with the content "Incorrect notification on UI at requesting a Password Reset Link when user reminder queries enabled" should be in position number "12"
	When I sort the changelog results in ascending order
	Then the changelog entry with the content "Incorrect notification on UI at requesting a Password Reset Link when user reminder queries enabled" should be in position number "1"
	And the changelog entry with the content "Anchor in portlet url does not work correctly" should be in position number "3"
	And the changelog entry with the content "Control Panel Instance Settings fields grayed out after clicking from Account Created Notification" should be in position number "6"
	And the changelog entry with the content "JS error when selecting pagination limit" should be in position number "7"
	And the changelog entry with the content "AlloyEditor toolbar for table editing is misplaced when content field was half visible" should be in position number "10"
	When I sort the changelog results in descending order
	Then the changelog entry with the content "AlloyEditor toolbar for table editing is misplaced when content field was half visible" should be in position number "1"
	And the changelog entry with the content "Control Panel Instance Settings fields grayed out after clicking from Account Created Notification" should be in position number "6"
	And the changelog entry with the content "JS error when selecting pagination limit" should be in position number "7"
	And the changelog entry with the content "Anchor in portlet url does not work correctly" should be in position number "9"
	And the changelog entry with the content "Incorrect notification on UI at requesting a Password Reset Link when user reminder queries enabled" should be in position number "12"
	When I clear all search refinements
	And I refine the current search using the following refinement criteria
	| Contains Text | Security Vulnerabilities |
	Then the changelog entry with the content "Security vulnerabilities in Apache Batik" should be in position number "1"
	And the changelog entry with the content "Security vulnerabilities in Apache PDFBox" should be in position number "2"
	And the changelog entry with the content "Security vulnerabilities in Spring core" should be in position number "5"
	And the changelog entry with the content "Security vulnerabilities in Netty" should be in position number "7"
	And the changelog entry with the content "Security vulnerabilities in Apache Tika" should be in position number "8"
	When I sort the changelog results in ascending order
	Then the changelog entry with the content "Security vulnerabilities in Apache Tika" should be in position number "1"
	And the changelog entry with the content "Security vulnerabilities in Netty" should be in position number "3"
	And the changelog entry with the content "Security vulnerabilities in Apache Batik" should be in position number "4"
	And the changelog entry with the content "Security vulnerabilities in Apache PDFBox" should be in position number "5"
	And the changelog entry with the content "Security vulnerabilities in Spring core" should be in position number "8"
	When I sort the changelog results in descending order
	Then the changelog entry with the content "Security vulnerabilities in Apache Batik" should be in position number "1"
	And the changelog entry with the content "Security vulnerabilities in Apache PDFBox" should be in position number "2"
	And the changelog entry with the content "Security vulnerabilities in Spring core" should be in position number "5"
	And the changelog entry with the content "Security vulnerabilities in Netty" should be in position number "7"
	And the changelog entry with the content "Security vulnerabilities in Apache Tika" should be in position number "8"

